    "Description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: xfrm: espintcp: do not reuse an in-progress partial send (CVE-2026-52935)\n\n* kernel: USB: serial: io_ti: fix heap overflow in get_manuf_info() (CVE-2026-53196)\n\n* kernel: sctp: keep chunk-\u003etransport in step with the list it is queued on (CVE-2026-74588)\n\n* kernel: sctp: validate cookie AUTH state before use (CVE-2026-74752)\n\n* kernel: smb: client: reject a tree connect response whose byte count is too small (CVE-2026-89631)\n\n* kernel: sctp: stop processing a packet once its association is deleted (CVE-2026-89479)\n\n* kernel: perf: Fix addr_filter_ranges lifetime (CVE-2026-93817)\n\n* kernel: netfilter: nfnetlink_log: wait for rcu grace period before freeing pernet state (CVE-2026-93288)\n\n* kernel: kernel: strparser: use-after-free via msg_timer_work rearm after strp_done() cancellation ()\n\n* kernel: netfilter: flowtable: hold reference on ct until flow is released (CVE-2026-98320)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n*  gfs2 filesystem withdrawal rework [RHEL-8] (JIRA:RHEL-129363)\n\n* Batch: z-stream xfrm - rhel-8.10.z (NST-Core-26W38) (JIRA:RHEL-256684)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
